{"step_index":75,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:11:28Z","thinking":"**Re-examining Export Feedback**\n\nRe-reading the request to ensure complete understanding of the requirements regarding the ledger export issues. The prompt specifies missing rows or excessive export times for large workspaces. Determine the precise next action by considering what was previously delivered.\n\n\n**Analyzing Export Problem Reports**\n\nThe `brief.md` document outlines the responsibility for large exports, owned by Sam, and its current active status. The goal is to improve the reliability and usability of customer data exports, specifically for large workspaces. Support reports missing rows or slow exports. Examine relevant evidence to understand prior actions and determine the next logical step.\n\n\n**Evaluating Async Export Rollout**\n\nThe async export feature was deployed on August 25th, based on the record details. The \"14 days old\" feature age from the support dashboard refers to the days since rollout, not the age of the ticket. The initial deployment included a smoke test that passed, and addressed using a background worker. Adding progress wording was a later release on September 5th.\n\n\n**Correlating Export Failures with Evidence**\n\nThe provided information establishes that both tickets relate to exports occurring *after* the async rollout. Ticket `record-f10fee8e5d` involves a CSV export with an expired link, matching evidence `record-eb2ad86fcb`, showing a 403 status after a 19.7-minute generation time. The URL TTL (15 minutes) is less than the generation time, explaining the expiration. It will be helpful to examine the system's URL generation.\n\n\n**Investigating Export Inconsistencies**\n\nThe first reported issue involves an expired download link due to a TTL shorter than the export time. The export worker completed, however the link expired before the download could begin, resulting in a 403 error. The second case reveals missing rows in an NDJSON export, confirmed by a warning about resuming an account relation scan after a cursor checkpoint.\n\nThe incomplete NDJSON export data indicates that there are cases of data loss. This also corroborates with another support ticket.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport os, glob\n\n# Check for all json files in evidence\njson_files = glob.glob(\"/workspace/product/history/evidence/*.json\")\nprint(\"JSON files in evidence:\", json_files)\n\n# Check all files in evidence that mention export, ferry, dump, ledger, 7c21733985, signed_url, checkpoint\nevidence_files = glob.glob(\"/workspace/product/history/evidence/*\")\nprint(f\"Total evidence files: {len(evidence_files)}\")\n\nrelevant = []\nfor f in evidence_files:\n    with open(f) as fh:\n        text = fh.read()\n        # look for references to 7c21733985, e733dfbdc6, c81238c2b3, or large export\n        if \"7c21733985\" in text or \"e733dfbdc6\" in text or \"c81238c2b3\" in text or \"large-export\" in text or \"Large\" in text:\n            relevant.append((f, text[:200]))\n\nprint(f\"Relevant evidence files: {len(relevant)}\")\nfor f, preview in relevant:\n    print(f, \"-->\", preview.replace(\"\\n\", \" \"))\n'","Cwd":"/workspace","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Searching all evidence files","toolSummary":"Search evidence files for relevant records"}}]}
