{"step_index":89,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:11:50Z","thinking":"**Identifying Relevant Actions**\n\nOnly two actions within the codebase involve the target functionality. One is a legacy, chunked export approach (`record-c0268a81ef`), and the other is a newer asynchronous export system (`record-7c21733985`). The newer system appears to replace the earlier one, and is signed.\n\n\n**Analyzing Export Job Evidence**\n\nThe recent release introduced \"Preparing your export\" wording, but didn't involve changes to worker behavior, row selection, checkpoints, or signed URLs. Evidence points to the newer export system (`record-7c21733985`) being tested with varied results. One test produced a 403 error due to URL expiration; another had a missing row count, and a third involved a dashboard correction.\n\n\n**Examining Support Ticket Data**\n\nTwo support tickets describe large export failures. One indicates a 403 error due to URL expiration after successful export generation. The other reports a record count discrepancy between the estimated and imported rows.\n\nChecking for additional tickets or evidence of similar issues among other files from `history/support` now.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport os, glob\n\nfiles = sorted(glob.glob(\"/workspace/product/history/support/*\"))\nprint(f\"Total support files: {len(files)}\")\nfor f in files:\n    with open(f) as fh:\n        content = fh.read()\n        lines = [line.strip() for line in content.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n        header = lines[0] if lines else \"\"\n        sub = [l for l in lines if \"Subject:\" in l]\n        sub = sub[0] if sub else \"\"\n        cohort = [l for l in lines if \"Cohort:\" in l]\n        cohort = cohort[0] if cohort else \"\"\n        subm = [l for l in lines if \"Submitted:\" in l]\n        subm = subm[0] if subm else \"\"\n        impm = [l for l in lines if \"Imported: